course: dictionary
lesson: 2447
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the sentence tells you which one to use. Dance can mean to move your body to music, or it can mean a party. Look at the words around it to decide.
explain: «Ruby taught her dad the moves, and he danced like a wardrobe falling down the stairs, but he kept going, laughing louder every round.» Taught the moves and laughing tell you danced means moved his body to music, in a funny way.
explain: «Chloe switches the dance game off mid-song when she's losing to Aisha.» Dance here names a game you play by moving to music. Ask yourself what word would fit, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: As a verb, dance means to move your body to music.
fact: As a noun, a dance is one set of steps, like a waltz or a tap dance.
fact: A dance can also be a party where people dance, like «the lobsters went to the dance».
fact: Dance can also mean the art of dancing, like ballet.
fact: Bees do a dance to show other bees where the flowers are.
exercise: «Ruby taught her dad the moves, and he danced like a wardrobe falling down the stairs.» What does danced mean here? | *Moved his body to music, in a funny way | Taught the moves to the children | Fell down the stairs | Sang loudly at a party
exercise: «They went with the lobsters to the dance.» What does dance mean here? | A kind of bee | *A party where people dance | One set of steps, like a waltz | To move your body to music
exercise: Dance class lasts 45 minutes, and Aisha goes to 4 classes each week. How many minutes is that in total? | 190 | 145 | 225 | *180
test: What does dance mean in «Ballet is a kind of dance»? | *The art of dancing, with steps | A school lesson for PE | A party for children | To move your body to music
test: What does dance mean in «Dad loves to dance at weddings»? | A party with food | The art of ballet | *To move his body to music | One set of steps, like a waltz
exam: Ruby's class has a dance on Friday night. What is a dance here? | The art of ballet | A set of steps, like a tap dance | *A party where people dance | To move your body to music
